# Project Rules

## Core Principles

- Follow `PROJECT_MASTER_SPECIFICATION.md` as the single source of truth.
- Follow `docs/ROADMAP.md` for milestone sequencing and current status.
- Work incrementally — complete one milestone task at a time.
- Avoid implementing future milestones without explicit instruction.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies and technologies.
- Keep implementations simple and focused.
- Preserve existing working functionality.
- Update documentation when implementation changes require it.

## Scope Control

- Do not create application code, Dockerfiles, Kubernetes manifests, Helm charts, or CI/CD workflows until their respective milestones.
- Do not introduce technologies outside the approved stack without explicit approval.
- Do not over-engineer or add abstractions prematurely.

## Documentation

- Read relevant project documentation before making changes.
- Mark planned/unimplemented features clearly as "Planned" in documentation.
- Never claim future functionality is already implemented.

## Quality

- A task is not complete merely because code was written — it must be tested and verified.
- Never claim something works without verification.
- Never commit secrets or hardcoded credentials.
